    -- legacy 01a0e60f-4ca9-74e6-906e-31f32f3ff683 (active): Keep CI caches within the repository budget so main runs stay warm
    -- Main CI runs keep going cold because GitHub evicts their caches. The repository's live cache set is
    -- about 13.8 GB against a 10 GB budget. The seL4 build-output caches account for about 8.9 GB of that,
    -- in eight per-job partitions: four generation shards at 1.36 to 1.44 GB each, the product job at 1.53
    -- GB, and three 0.52 to 0.58 GB image-only jobs. The Nix store, Kani, MyQue, projection and rust-cache
    -- entries add about 4.9 GB. Every build-output key also carries the commit SHA, so each main run
    -- writes a new copy of every partition. Least-recently-used eviction then removes entries the next run
    -- needs, the Zutai evaluation stores and the 2 GB Nix store among them. Of the three main runs after
    -- 35ca61d that ran the seL4 jobs, one was warm (19 minutes), one was fully cold (30 minutes, at
    -- d0ec4ee), and one lost its contract-source evaluation store within 45 minutes of saving it.
    (h.planned "01a1b49c-aab1-7704-8548-abbcd7e6a4fe"
      "Jobs whose cached build outputs come from the same build restore one shared partition, and exactly one job saves it, so no two jobs race to save the same key. The four generation shards share one partition at the least. Every seL4 job still restores the build outputs it used to restore, so no job becomes a cold build."
      "Keep CI caches within the repository budget so main runs stay warm"
      "rehomed from a active item; unbound acceptance: regression-surface; only a human gate: needs an automated exam"
      {
        h.human "retention-observed" "ci-cache-retention" "An operator reads the main-branch CI runs after the implementation merges. A run qualifies if it runs the seL4 jobs to success without being cancelled, and if its head commit changes no build-output key input, Nix key input or contracts .zt file relative to the preceding qualifying run. A qualifying run is warm when every seL4 job restored its build-output partition and the Nix store, and both contract jobs restored their Zutai evaluation store. consecutiveWarmRuns counts consecutive warm qualifying runs, with no cold qualifying run between them, and must reach 3. slowestCriticalPathSeconds is the slowest of those runs, measured from its first job starting to the CI aggregate finishing, and is bounded by 1320 s. cacheUsageMegabytes is the repository's active cache size after the last counted run completes, as the Actions cache usage API reports it, and is bounded by 9000 MB. Record the last counted run's URL as the target.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a0e60f-4ca9-74e6-906e-31f32f3ff683"; }; };
    (h.planned "01a1b49c-aab1-7704-8548-abbd76c26c50"
      "A build-output partition's key binds its existing inputs (runner, toolchain and lockfiles, pins, seL4 configuration, linker scripts, submodule gitlinks) and the UTC date instead of the commit SHA. A run whose exact key already exists saves nothing for that partition. The first run of a day restores the previous day's entry by prefix and saves the new day's."
      "Keep CI caches within the repository budget so main runs stay warm"
