    -- legacy 01a130ec-7401-7674-893d-602ced3494de (open): Closure generation and resolution re-read the same inputs per closure
    -- Regenerating or checking the system-image closure corpus dominates the development loop. Measured on
    -- a warm zutai cache, generate-system-image-closures.py --check takes about 272 s: 200 s re-render
    -- computed system specs through the system-spec-source evaluator at 13-18 s per call, once per closure
    -- whose base is a computed system, and 59 s re-hash the same few workspace trees 1727 times.
    -- resolve_closure costs 1.7 s for an ordinary closure and 15-19 s for one over a computed system,
    -- because it re-admits the component-spec corpus twice and re-renders the computed source; each
    -- corpus-wide checker therefore spends minutes re-reading identical bytes. Chained through the closure
    -- gates this approaches an hour per regeneration.
    (h.planned "01a1b49c-ac07-758c-9557-0adae5c246a8"
      "Every committed closure and negative case is reproduced byte for byte: generate-system-image-closures.py --check passes against the corpus that exists before this change, and every tree digest it records is unchanged."
      "Closure generation and resolution re-read the same inputs per closure"
      "rehomed from a open item; unbound acceptance: closure-gates-pass"
      h.noAcceptance) with { supersedes = { "01a130ec-7401-7674-893d-602ced3494de"; }; };
