  }) with {
    nonGoals = {
      "Enabling every Cargo feature simultaneously, implementing protocols absent from the pinned smoltcp release, or a moving completion target tied to future releases.";
      "Ambient bind/connect/listen, wildcard or port-range client grants, raw packet injection/sniffing for ordinary applications, resolver-wide access, or trust/discovery responses that create authority.";
      "DDSI-RTPS discovery/reliability/CDR implementation, full Zenoh or ROS compatibility, transport security implementations, and physical NIC qualification; each is separately owned.";
      "Truncation and queue-bound policy, DDS endpoint profiles and multicast, which are separate slices.";
      "Ambient bind/connect/listen, wildcard or port-range grants, and raw-packet authority for ordinary applications.";
      "DDSI-RTPS discovery, reliability, history, CDR or QoS matching; multicast.";
      "Resolver-wide client access, DNSSEC or encrypted DNS, mDNS, or names authorizing an unrelated destination.";
      "IPv6 AAAA records before the IPv6 slices land.";
      "Raw ICMP or arbitrary ICMP types for ordinary clients, traceroute-style TTL control, or ICMP for IPv6 before that slice.";
      "IPv6 fragmentation, path MTU discovery, or 6LoWPAN fragmentation.";
      "Physical NIC, IOMMU or board qualification; QEMU evidence carries no hardware claim.";
      "SLAAC, router advertisement processing, IPv6 fragmentation, or TCP/UDP over IPv6, which are separate slices.";
      "Dual-stack name resolution policy beyond exact grants, or IPv6 multicast.";
      "DHCPv6, option-driven boot or configuration beyond address, mask, gateway and resolver, or leases widening any client grant.";
      "DHCPv6, privacy extensions beyond what the pinned release provides, or multi-router preference policy.";
      "Any multicast grant or protocol behavior in the network service, or a second verification framework.";
      "General LAN discovery, DDSI-RTPS or Zenoh scouting policy, IPv6 multicast listener discovery, or source-specific multicast beyond the declared sender policy.";
      "Implementing any excluded medium, or claiming a backend qualifies another board or NIC.";
      "Performance targets, denial-of-service resistance claims beyond declared bounds, or physical NIC behavior.";
      "New protocol behavior, or completion of any slice by aggregation alone.";
      "Removing a job's restore, a check or the pinned image build, or changing what any check asserts.";
      "Changing the Nix, Kani, MyQue, projection or rust-cache caches, or the Zutai evaluation store's key recipe.";
      "Buying cache storage or moving caches off GitHub Actions.";
      "Changing the closure contract, any closure identity, or the tree-digest encoding.";
      "Making the system-spec-source evaluator itself faster, or making system_spec_check faster.";
      "A cross-process render cache, parallel resolution, or factoring shared release inputs out of each closure.";
      "Any runtime, QEMU-plane or physical-machine claim.";
      "Changing product builds, seL4 build-output partitions, Cargo target directories, Kani or Rust caches, or Zutai evaluation-store keys.";
      "Introducing a new shell, changing compiler packaging or pins, buying storage, external cache services, or repository-wide cache scheduling and eviction.";
      "Granting broader workflow permissions, executing untrusted PR code in privileged jobs, enabling publication or deleting remote caches without separate operator authorization.";
      "Guaranteeing the historical 902313763-byte saving or the repository-wide 9000 MB retention target; those require independent measurements.";
      "Changing format 2, its checker, or anything the RPi5 ROS 2 demo plan claims.";
      "Retiring any other superseded contract version.";
      "Changing the generation format, the builder, or which manifests it declares.";
      "Retiring the retained v2-v4 schemas that check-contracts.py still type-checks.";
      "Controls for the corpus checker's own shard selection: it is verification tooling, which docs/decisions/negative-controls-for-product-judges.md exempts.";
      "Changing any schema, gen_rust.zt, or generated binding: the committed outputs are the reference this work is judged against and must not move.";
      "Folding the seven differing generators into the table.";
      "Changing the pinned Zutai toolchain or rustfmt edition.";
      "Judging what the idle ros2-demo-subscriber prints: it is in the composition and holds no network authority, and its output is neither required nor judged here. The exam reads the connector's lines only.";
      "Any peer but one eclipse-zenoh 1.0.0 wheel on x86_64 Linux, any other port, a router or client peer, rmw_zenoh interoperability, liveliness tokens, queryables, and fragmented messages.";
      "Inbound connections to the guest, a guest listener on a NIC, DNS, scouting of any kind, and a hostname destination.";
      "A physical NIC. QEMU user networking is the only link observed; its translation of the guest's connection to the host's loopback is not the wire a physical network would show.";
      "Running a stock peer in CI. The wheel comes from a registry, so the recipe is an explicit local experiment in no aggregate.";
      "Any product change in this item's planning PR: no system spec, no generated composition, no guest change, and no modified schema. They are the implementation's.";
      "Making a plane checker execute from its record. A later item owns that.";
      "Other checkers. This item covers only the network checker.";
      "Detecting a device that a run-time computation names without any device string in the code. No check here can.";
      "Any product change and any QEMU boot. This item makes no boot claim.";
      "Any change to the `system-test-run/v1` contract.";
    };
